WEBVTT

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:16.120
2/14 Tuesday

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:23.130
<i>I love stuff like this.</i>

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:27.330
<i>Everyone's been drawing 
Valentine's Day stuff.</i>

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.850
<i>What an excellent service.</i>

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:38.880
<i>I was trying to calm my nerves 
by looking at some illustrations,</i>

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:43.000
<i>but I think I might be even more nervous now.</i>

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:13.980
Koikimo

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:18.990
Episode 8

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:18.990
"The Person I Love Is..."

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:21.240
Amakusa

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:23.870
Uh, Onii-chan...

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:24.620
<b>Sei</b>

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:25.370
<b>za</b>

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:28.890
<b>Seiza</b>

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:28.710
Do you really need to wait by the door?

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:30.850
Of course I do! I want to wait outside,

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:31.020
<b>Grar</b>

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:34.000
but the neighbors would think I'm 
a creeper, so I'm waiting here!

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:34.900
Yeah, sure.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:36.770
You do you.

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:43.510
<i>He looks like a pet waiting 
for his master to come home.</i>

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:52.000
Hello!

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:56.950
G-Good morning...

00:02:57.570 --> 00:02:59.080
Good morning.

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:03.710
Ichika-san, you look a bit pale.

00:03:03.710 --> 00:03:05.490
I just didn't get much sleep.

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:07.240
Er, well, come in.

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:12.290
Would you like to sit down for a bit?

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:13.130
No.

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:15.170
You could lie down on the sofa.

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:17.170
No, really. I'm fine.

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:22.600
I-I came over today to give 
you a Valentine's Day gift...

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:28.100
Uh, what's with the hands?

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.740
Ready to accept my chocolate at any time.

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:33.580
You're so annoying, it's almost refreshing.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:37.530
I'm not here to give you chocolate.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:40.570
I spent a few days trying to 
figure out what to give you.

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:45.450
I kept thinking... and before I 
knew it, it was Valentine's Day.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:48.640
I know I'm going to regret it...

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:51.960
but I'm going to do it.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:57.590
This is what I decided to do!

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:08.560
There! That's my Valentine's Day gift to you!

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:12.250
I tried to avoid chocolates, 
and this is what happened!

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:15.760
I will not be taking any thoughts 
or comments on this matter, ever!

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:17.800
Now, if you'll excuse me!

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:25.070
Oh, did Ichika leave?

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:26.760
I was gonna go to school with her—

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:31.130
What are you doing?

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:34.000
Did she tackle you?

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:38.050
She gave me something far more destructive.

00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:41.340
Well, judging by your reaction,

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:43.530
it must've made you really happy.

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:45.050
It did.

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:50.900
She's so cute...

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:56.350
Anyway, I'm heading out, 
so make sure you lock the door.

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:54.900
She's so cute...

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:03.900
<i>She seemed pretty adamant 
about not giving me chocolate.</i>

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:07.850
<i>Masuda must've said something to her.</i>

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:21.860
It only took a second for me to completely 
change my opinion about Valentine's.

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:27.800
I'm so sorry, Rio.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:30.780
We should've just walked to school together.

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:32.010
Don't worry about it.

00:05:32.530 --> 00:05:35.290
By the way, my brother seemed pretty happy.

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:37.810
He was writhing by the front door.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:40.840
I... I see...

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:42.190
Why is your speech so stilted?

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:45.290
I'm going to die from embarrassment 
just thinking about it.

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:46.780
Oh, yeah.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:49.490
Here, Rio. Your BFF chocolate.

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:51.350
Oh, sweet. Thanks.

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:52.420
My mom's snoring is insane.

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:56.880
I can hear her next door. 
She's so frickin' loud.

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:55.830
Ru-chan, Sacchan, here!

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:57.380
Wow, thanks.

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:58.350
Yay!

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:59.960
I couldn't sleep at all yesterday.

00:05:58.350 --> 00:05:59.200
Here.

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:02.430
And here's one from me.

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:04.970
Wow, this looks so good. Did you make these?

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:05.420
The girls seem to be having fun.

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:06.040
And here.

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:08.280
The packaging is so cute!

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:08.280
It looks delicious.

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:13.720
Right? The chocolates inside 
are super cute, too.

00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:10.770
So cute!

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:17.230
So I finally got super pissed,

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:20.730
2/14 Tuesday

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:20.730
Arima Ichika

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:20.730
Do you have some time at lunch today?

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:20.730
Display

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:19.220
and we got into a fight.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:23.450
What're you looking at?

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:25.190
Nothing...

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:26.880
Why are you smirking?

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:29.000
What? I'm not.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:29.620
Lemme see!

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:31.490
Dude, get off of me!

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:33.210
You're looking at something 
pervy, aren't you?

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:34.990
No!

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:37.900
Come on! Show me!

00:06:42.950 --> 00:06:45.500
Sorry to ask you to meet with me at lunch.

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:48.370
I thought about giving it to you in class,

00:06:48.370 --> 00:06:50.680
but I thought you might not like that.

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:55.470
It's also to thank you for 
letting me borrow the books,

00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:57.350
but I hope you enjoy them.

00:06:59.450 --> 00:07:01.590
Anyway, uh... I'll see you later.

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:03.330
Hang on a sec.

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:06.670
Oh, do you not like chocolate?

00:07:06.670 --> 00:07:08.940
No, that's not it.

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:13.450
You're giving this to 
me as a friend... right?

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:17.660
I, uh...

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:19.510
Really?

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:23.250
It's a secret, so don't 
go blabbing it to people.

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:24.250
Yeah, yeah.

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:26.670
Wow, that was reassuring.

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:28.610
You're probably going to tell someone.

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:30.310
Don't worry.

00:07:30.310 --> 00:07:32.560
U-Um...

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:37.140
If I said I would've preferred something only 
for me rather than something obligatory...

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:38.430
would you get mad?

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:42.720
I, uh... Does that mean...

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:45.060
What I'm getting at is...

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:48.450
I want you to go out with me.

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:54.070
U-Um... I...

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:59.310
I've never looked at you 
in that way... so, um...

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:01.080
Then could you start?

00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:03.330
Think it over, okay?

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:09.380
You can take your time replying. I'll wait.

00:08:10.410 --> 00:08:12.840
Anyway, I'm gonna head back to class.

00:08:13.310 --> 00:08:15.170
Thanks for the chocolates.

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:33.350
<i>When should I give Amakusa his chocolates?</i>

00:08:33.350 --> 00:08:35.470
<i>Lunch break is almost over.</i>

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:37.570
<b>H
m
m
m
.
.
.</b>

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:38.100
Hey, Arrietty, are you listening?

00:08:39.250 --> 00:08:42.090
Huh? No, sorry. I wasn't.

00:08:42.090 --> 00:08:48.080
Again... Acting Section Chief Amakusa 
won't accept chocolate from anyone.

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:49.860
Huh? Wait, seriously?

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:50.590
Yeah.

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:55.780
Last year, one of the newer girls tried to 
give him chocolate, and he wouldn't take it.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:59.720
This year, another girl tried 
and the same thing happened,

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:01.570
so this rumor's definitely true.

00:09:01.570 --> 00:09:03.500
I-I see...

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:05.610
Surprising, right?

00:09:05.610 --> 00:09:10.400
I always figured he was 
drowning in valentines.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:12.350
Maybe he doesn't like chocolate.

00:09:12.350 --> 00:09:14.320
Yeah, I'm not sure.

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:17.070
<i>H-He won't take them?</i>

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:19.340
<i>I've never heard this before!</i>

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:22.330
Wait, Arrietty...

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:25.600
Were you planning to give him chocolate?

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:28.300
Huh?! N-No way!

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:30.740
Yeah, of course not.

00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:34.140
<i>Maybe I'll just take this 
chocolate back home with me...</i>

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:36.860
So I went to this dessert 
buffet the other day...

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:38.540
<i>Nay!</i>

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:47.750
<b>Menacing</b>

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:42.230
<i>I made up my mind that I was gonna do this!</i>

00:09:42.230 --> 00:09:44.450
<i>It's fine if he lets me down! 
I'm giving it to him!</i>

00:09:42.380 --> 00:09:44.450
That place was amazing!

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:46.760
Especially the peach mousse 
I had. You <i>have</i> to try it.

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:47.260
<i>I want Amakusa to know 
that I at least tried!</i>

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:48.350
The plates were fancy, too.

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:50.540
So colorful and pretty.

00:09:48.860 --> 00:09:53.030
<i>Wait. Maybe he'll accept something 
that's not chocolate.</i>

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:55.240
Let's go together sometime! 
Nothing beats enjoying sweets.

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:55.240
<i>Maybe I still have time to go buy something!</i>

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:57.740
Crap! Look at the time!

00:09:58.310 --> 00:09:59.160
Huh?

00:09:59.390 --> 00:10:01.410
Arrietty, we have to hurry back!

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:03.730
No way! I have a meeting!

00:10:03.730 --> 00:10:05.180
Come on! Hurry!

00:10:10.970 --> 00:10:12.920
<i>I never got to give it to him...</i>

00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:14.930
<i>On top of all the meetings,</i>

00:10:14.930 --> 00:10:18.010
<i>I had a bunch of routine 
work to get done today, too.</i>

00:10:19.530 --> 00:10:24.040
<i>I totally lost sight of Amakusa 
while I was doing overtime.</i>

00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:27.390
<i>Looks like I got all worked up 
for nothing this Valentine's.</i>

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:33.650
<i>That height and figure...</i>

00:10:34.090 --> 00:10:36.410
<i>Is that... Amakusa?!</i>

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:38.760
<i>W-Wait a sec!</i>

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:42.040
<i>Oh, no! He's going!</i>

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:43.590
Amakusa!

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:52.040
<i>Of all the times... Seriously?</i>

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:54.300
<i>I'm so stupid!</i>

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:55.190
Matsushima?

00:10:56.270 --> 00:10:58.150
What's up? Everything okay?

00:11:00.170 --> 00:11:01.550
I'll head over there.

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:03.160
Wait!

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:06.540
C-Come this way.

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:08.530
It'll just take a sec!

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:17.030
Here. Valentine's Day chocolate.

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:18.630
I really wanted to give it to you.

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:21.910
I-I heard you don't accept chocolate,

00:11:22.230 --> 00:11:25.090
so I thought about trying to 
get you something else, but...

00:11:25.090 --> 00:11:28.160
Sorry! I just didn't have any time!

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:32.040
So I wanted to give this to you, 
even if you rejected it...

00:11:32.470 --> 00:11:35.230
But I just couldn't get to you at all today.

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:39.800
And then this... Ugh! I can't 
keep my thoughts straight!

00:11:44.740 --> 00:11:48.130
Thanks for running over to give me these.

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:55.560
<i>The train bound for Shibuya and Shinjuku 
will be arriving soon on track 2.</i>

00:11:55.890 --> 00:11:59.320
<i>For your safety, please stand 
behind the yellow line.</i>

00:12:09.260 --> 00:12:11.980
I want you to go out with me.

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:14.370
Then could you start?

00:12:14.620 --> 00:12:16.150
Think it over, okay?

00:12:19.450 --> 00:12:21.340
What should I do?

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:33.020
Koikimo

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:33.020
I got tons of
chocolates from
my juniors.

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:33.020
<b>Smug</b>

00:12:35.820 --> 00:12:37.270
Excuse me.

00:12:37.540 --> 00:12:38.860
<b>Literature Club
in Session!</b>

00:12:39.310 --> 00:12:41.340
Sorry to interrupt your club work.

00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:43.620
My name's Amakusa.

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:49.080
I'd like to talk to Tamaru 
for a little while. You mind?

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:51.190
Um...

00:12:51.190 --> 00:12:53.520
Well, you heard her, Tamaru-kun...

00:12:53.520 --> 00:12:55.760
May I be excused for a bit, President?

00:12:55.760 --> 00:12:57.320
Y-Yeah.

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:09.220
There's definitely something going on there!

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:11.060
Something is afoot.

00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:12.950
Is she asking him out?

00:13:12.950 --> 00:13:14.380
Maybe they're fighting.

00:13:16.810 --> 00:13:19.820
<b>Literature Club
in Session!</b>

00:13:17.180 --> 00:13:19.820
I wanna know!

00:13:21.420 --> 00:13:22.820
<b>Green
Tea</b>

00:13:28.310 --> 00:13:29.610
Why don't you sit?

00:13:29.610 --> 00:13:31.330
Nah, I'm good.

00:13:31.670 --> 00:13:32.860
I'll stand.

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:33.910
Fine.

00:13:39.450 --> 00:13:43.710
Ichika's been acting weird ever 
since lunch on Valentine's Day.

00:13:45.290 --> 00:13:49.920
When I ask her if anything happened, 
she just brushes it off and won't tell me.

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:53.600
I figured you might know something.

00:13:55.760 --> 00:13:57.770
I guess you could say that.

00:13:58.320 --> 00:14:00.020
I'm actually probably the reason.

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:03.010
Because I asked Arima out.

00:14:04.130 --> 00:14:05.120
I knew it.

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:06.730
I mean...

00:14:06.730 --> 00:14:09.440
You called me out here because 
you figured that's what it was.

00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:10.480
Yeah.

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:13.790
Huh...

00:14:14.610 --> 00:14:17.540
You even said that wasn't 
how you felt before.

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:21.160
I wasn't sure how I felt back then!

00:14:21.690 --> 00:14:23.000
But now...

00:14:28.230 --> 00:14:31.240
I know how I feel.

00:14:32.690 --> 00:14:33.880
That's why I asked her out.

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:36.690
I see.

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:41.230
Hey, Amakusa.

00:14:41.720 --> 00:14:45.310
Did you ask me this because 
you're worried about Arima?

00:14:45.930 --> 00:14:47.490
Yeah, why?

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:49.550
What are you getting at?

00:14:49.550 --> 00:14:53.120
Then I'll just be honest here.
From my perspective,

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:55.170
you're a busybody, Amakusa.

00:14:56.920 --> 00:15:00.480
What? I was just worried because 
Ichika was acting weird.

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:05.830
She usually tells me everything, 
but this time...

00:15:05.830 --> 00:15:06.940
Amakusa...

00:15:08.690 --> 00:15:09.950
Maybe you're lonely.

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:31.150
Me asking Amakusa out has 
nothing to do with you.

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:32.530
It doesn't...

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:35.910
does it?

00:15:38.990 --> 00:15:41.910
Yeah... You're right.

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:46.300
Whatever Ichika decides to do is up to her,

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:48.550
so it technically doesn't concern me.

00:15:50.650 --> 00:15:56.020
Maybe you should just be there for her 
when Arima actually asks for help.

00:15:56.020 --> 00:15:59.530
You're surprisingly blunt, Tamaru.

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:01.900
Not as blunt as you.

00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:06.870
Then I guess you're going to end 
up being my brother's rival.

00:16:06.870 --> 00:16:07.720
Yeah.

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:12.950
<b>Green
Tea</b>

00:16:16.140 --> 00:16:19.690
Oh? You really think you're up to the task?

00:16:21.180 --> 00:16:24.620
Stop it. I can feel my confidence draining.

00:16:32.430 --> 00:16:33.290
<i>Ichika-san?</i>

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:37.220
Oh, sorry. Um...

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:40.260
We were talking about the gym 
class you mentioned yesterday.

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:43.660
You were playing basketball today, right?

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:47.680
<i>Oh, yeah. Rio and I ended up 
on different teams today.</i>

00:16:47.680 --> 00:16:50.070
<i>I could barely keep up...</i>

00:16:52.370 --> 00:16:54.400
Well... Goodnight.

00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:08.670
<i>Tamaru-kun is nice, cool, 
and probably a good person.</i>

00:17:09.140 --> 00:17:14.370
<i>And we'd be able to talk about the 
things we like and even trivial things.</i>

00:17:14.370 --> 00:17:16.780
<i>Of course, I don't dislike him.</i>

00:17:17.790 --> 00:17:21.530
<i>Honestly, I'm happy he asked me out.</i>

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:26.410
<i>But... I don't think I like him that way.</i>

00:17:28.300 --> 00:17:31.990
<i>Is it because I see him as a friend?</i>

00:17:35.760 --> 00:17:40.400
<i>Or... is the person I like...</i>

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:47.160
Are you stalking me again?

00:17:47.160 --> 00:17:51.340
You haven't sounded like yourself 
on the phone these past few days...

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:53.110
I was worried, so I came to check on you.

00:17:53.110 --> 00:17:57.860
Okay, but could you not wait 
for me near the school?

00:17:57.860 --> 00:18:01.690
Sorry, I was so worried, 
I couldn't help myself.

00:18:02.860 --> 00:18:04.600
Is something bothering you?

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:07.180
I'd be more than happy to listen.

00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:09.310
<i>Listen, huh?</i>

00:18:09.820 --> 00:18:16.060
<i>I wonder if Ryo-san's ever been asked out 
by someone he considered a friend.</i>

00:18:17.260 --> 00:18:21.220
<i>No... I'd rather not know.</i>

00:18:21.790 --> 00:18:23.540
No, I'm fine.

00:18:23.770 --> 00:18:26.090
I appreciate the concern.

00:18:26.090 --> 00:18:31.540
Well, it's usually easier to process 
anything bothering you if you verbalize it.

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:35.080
And it might be something 
I can help you with.

00:18:35.820 --> 00:18:37.720
Really, I'm fine.

00:18:37.940 --> 00:18:38.470
But—

00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:39.470
Ryo-san!

00:18:40.310 --> 00:18:42.310
Could you just stop?!

00:18:42.310 --> 00:18:44.420
Yes, I have something on my mind,

00:18:44.420 --> 00:18:46.840
but can't you take the hint 
that I don't want to tell you?

00:18:47.740 --> 00:18:49.350
You're always like this!

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:55.610
<b>Residential vehicles

00:18:50.030 --> 00:18:53.720
You always ignore how I feel, 
and it's always one-sided...

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:55.610
And...

00:18:56.110 --> 00:18:59.880
This is my problem, 
so it doesn't concern you.

00:19:02.550 --> 00:19:04.780
And I can't accept that.

00:19:04.780 --> 00:19:08.300
This is what I meant about 
everything being one-sided!

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:12.770
It's true that I don't often 
listen to what you have to say,

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:16.550
but at least let me worry about you!

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:19.890
No, that's just a front.

00:19:20.770 --> 00:19:23.780
I want your problems to be mine, Ichika-san.

00:19:27.090 --> 00:19:30.780
Why... are you so unreasonable?

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:34.840
Because I love you, Ichika-san.

00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:43.450
You're like some pushy 
door-to-door salesman.

00:19:43.990 --> 00:19:46.250
That's quite the analogy.

00:19:48.030 --> 00:19:50.500
Sorry, I was a bit harsh.

00:19:50.970 --> 00:19:53.880
And I sounded a bit harsh myself.

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:57.100
But I hope you understand that

00:19:57.890 --> 00:19:59.130
I'm not lying or joking.

00:20:00.790 --> 00:20:05.510
This is a problem that I need 
to figure out on my own,

00:20:05.960 --> 00:20:08.330
so could you just watch and wait?

00:20:14.130 --> 00:20:14.730
Okay.

00:20:26.410 --> 00:20:30.000
Um... Could you move your hand already?

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:33.460
I can't. Love's pull is just too powerful!

00:20:42.500 --> 00:20:46.550
<i>The reason I can't move 
forward with Tamaru-kun...</i>

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:49.220
<i>really is because of him.</i>

00:20:52.380 --> 00:20:56.400
<i>He's so one-sided, selfish, 
and annoyingly flashy.</i>

00:20:57.070 --> 00:21:00.970
<i>He's illogical, and he doesn't 
care much about others.</i>

00:21:00.970 --> 00:21:03.860
<i>He's always extra in everything he does...</i>

00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:08.620
<i>And he tries to justify 
everything with "love."</i>

00:21:09.300 --> 00:21:11.120
<i>We're so far apart in age...</i>

00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:15.120
<i>And he's a bad adult...</i>

00:21:15.440 --> 00:21:17.380
<i>I think all of this is true...</i>

00:21:19.980 --> 00:21:24.810
<i>but whenever I think of the word 
"love," I end up thinking of him.</i>

00:21:25.440 --> 00:21:27.740
Is something the matter? You've stopped.

00:21:28.370 --> 00:21:29.820
It's nothing.

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:34.090
<i>I can't fall for him, though.</i>

00:21:34.560 --> 00:21:38.920
<i>Logically, I know that Tamaru-kun 
would be better for me.</i>

00:21:39.910 --> 00:21:42.070
<i>Ugh, I'm such an idiot.</i>

00:21:42.540 --> 00:21:43.770
<i>Seriously.</i>

00:21:46.850 --> 00:21:50.670
<i>Still, it'd be really rude of me 
to leave Tamaru-kun hanging,</i>

00:21:51.770 --> 00:21:54.260
<i>so I need to tell him how I feel,</i>

00:21:55.790 --> 00:22:00.030
<i>since he told me how he felt so 
earnestly while looking into my eyes.</i>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.250
Next Time

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.250
"My Answer"

00:23:36.060 --> 00:23:38.450
Next time, "My Answer."
